  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Bahn Yard Office",
    "overview": "The Control Room lives inside Bahn's own visual world: the bahn.com vehicle transport page is the binding reference, so the system is warm birch paper, asphalt ink and sand-toned panels, with every control shaped as a pill. It reads as a calm operations desk, not a dashboard. Surfaces are flat tonal layers of sand on birch; there are almost no lines and almost no shadows, and hierarchy comes from tone, size and weight.\n\nType carries the brand. One wide, heavy, uppercase display cut names the page and the car, and nothing else. Everything an operator reads to decide (reasons, dates, routes, counts) is set in a friendly humanist sans with tabular figures, at sizes that stay legible on a daylight laptop and on a projector. Colour is semantic and rare: orange and red belong to the route's two ends and to risk; teal means live work; green means delivered. The ground stays quiet so those signals can be found at a glance.\n\nDensity is medium. Lists are stacks of rounded sand cards separated by small gaps, the selected item inverts to asphalt, and detail opens in a large sand panel beside the list, not in a modal.\n\nThe tokens are defined as custom properties in `starter/app/globals.css`, the fonts load through next/font in `starter/app/layout.tsx`, and the signature pieces live in `starter/app/components/shell.tsx`, `starter/app/components/card.tsx`, `starter/app/components/route-line.tsx` and `starter/app/components/record/header.tsx`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Birch ground, sand panels, asphalt ink; depth by tone, not shadow.",
      "Pill geometry for every control, 24px radius for large panels.",
      "Wide 900-weight uppercase display for page titles and car names only.",
      "Figtree with tabular figures for all working text.",
      "Orange pickup, red delivery and critical, teal live, green delivered.",
      "Selection is inversion to asphalt."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Signals Mean Something Rule",
        "body": "Orange, red, teal and green appear only where they encode pickup, delivery or critical, risk, live work, or done. They are never decoration, and a hue never swaps roles.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Is The Accent Rule",
        "body": "The action colour is asphalt, not a brand hue. Primary buttons, the pressed filter and the selected card are all ink on birch inverted.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wash-For-Fill Rule",
        "body": "Signal hues fill a surface only through their wash (`*-bg`) with their ink shade as text; the saturated 500 shade is reserved for dots, pins and progress.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Names Rule",
        "body": "The wide display cut is used for exactly two things: the page title and the car's name. Section heads, numbers, buttons and labels are Figtree.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Tabular figures are on at the root; times, counts and distances must align in every list.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tone Not Shadow Rule",
        "body": "A surface is separated from its parent by a step in the sand ramp. Do not add drop shadows to cards or panels.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Dark Panel Rule",
        "body": "Asphalt Panel is the only dark surface besides the selected-card inversion; it appears once per order page, overlapping the foot of the 3:1 car image by 96px (40px on small screens).",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build every control as a 999px pill: asphalt primary, Sand 100 tertiary, Sand 50 fields and tracks.",
      "**Do** separate surfaces by stepping the sand ramp (birch, Sand 50, Sand 100) rather than with borders or shadows.",
      "**Do** mark selection by inverting to asphalt with birch text and the on-dark signal tints.",
      "**Do** keep orange for pickup and risk, red for delivery and critical, teal for live work, green for delivered.",
      "**Do** set times, counts and distances in Figtree with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** use the 3px Stone focus ring on every interactive element and honour reduced motion by removing animation."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use the wide Archivo display for anything but page titles and car names.",
      "**Don't** fill a surface with a saturated signal hue; use its wash with its ink shade as text.",
      "**Don't** drop-shadow cards or panels; shadows are limited to the current-tab lift, the sticky action edge, inset hairlines and pin halos.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second dark surface beyond the selected-card inversion and the order page's Asphalt Panel.",
      "**Don't** use square or lightly rounded controls; buttons, fields, filters and pills are always full pills.",
      "**Don't** present the car illustration as a photo of the car; it always carries its \"Model illustration\" note."
    ]
  }
}